  "measurement_notes": [
    "Total event counts are per project, evenly divided among the selected number of streams. Receipt counts are included in each case.",
    "Capture/reconcile operate on the final stream; status covers all streams; resume follows the binding replacement chain (all four streams in these fixtures).",
    "100 and 1000 event cases use three uninstrumented timing samples per version; 5000 uses one. JSON/read counts use a separate instrumented invocation.",
    "The 5000-event single-stream capture case was measured in a separate earlier run from the other final cases; every final case uses the identical candidate source SHA-256.",
    "The initial pre-optimization 5000-event single-stream baseline capture observation was 12.53674980008509 seconds, above the configured 10-second hook timeout. The final safe candidate still measured 12.650000200024806 seconds in its separate capture run.",
    "All comparisons check complete return values and, for capture/reconcile, the exact written JSON bytes after fixing generated IDs and time. This is stable-fixture equivalence, not a claim of identical handling of concurrent mutations.",
    "Every candidate record read retains fresh checks of the full ancestor chain and per-file identity checks; no persistent index or record-format migration is introduced.",
    "The 10-second configuration is not a measured native-host execution guarantee. Native forced termination and residual lock behavior were not tested in this benchmark."
  ]
}
